Scope and permission

In this licence, the Framework means the project-authored XLL Python
software, including its compiler, runtime, IDE integration and any
modifications to those components. Each copyright holder grants you a
worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to use, study, copy and
modify the Framework for any purpose, including business use, and to
distribute it in source or binary form on the terms below. Private use
and modification carry no obligation to distribute source.

Distribution

1. You may distribute the Framework itself only free of charge. This
   applies to unchanged copies, forks, and renamed, rebuilt or
   repackaged versions. You may sell an independently authored add-in
   that includes the Framework as provided in LICENSE-PACKAGE-EXCEPTIONS.txt,
   which is part of this licence.

2. With every copy you distribute that includes all or part of the
   Framework, preserve its copyright notices, include this licence and
   LICENSE-PACKAGE-EXCEPTIONS.txt, and grant recipients the same rights
   under these terms for the Framework and your modifications to it.
   Additional product terms must preserve those rights.

3. Give each recipient the matching Framework source, including any
   modifications and build scripts needed to build the Framework portion,
   free of charge. You may supply it with the distribution or provide a
   working download link alongside the copy. A link to the exact upstream
   version suffices for an unmodified Framework. Source for an independent
   add-in is governed by the package exception.

